== Claim: for every n, k: linear C of length n, dual distance > k, |C| <= (2n)^ceil(k/2)
  n <= 31, all k <= n, two coordinate choices each: failures = 0; max of ln|C| - ceil(k/2) ln(2n) = 0.000 (<= 0 means the bound holds)
== Odd k: extended-BCH duals have dual distance >= 2t+2 > k = 2t+1 and size <= 2 (2^m)^t
  m=3 t=1: length 8, |C_ext|=2^4 (<= 2*8^1=2^4), dual distance=4 (> k=3: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 256; Rao M_t = 9
  m=3 t=2: length 8, |C_ext|=2^7 (<= 2*8^2=2^7), dual distance=8 (> k=5: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 4096; Rao M_t = 37
  m=3 t=3: length 8, |C_ext|=2^7 (<= 2*8^3=2^10), dual distance=8 (> k=7: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 65536; Rao M_t = 93
  m=4 t=1: length 16, |C_ext|=2^5 (<= 2*16^1=2^5), dual distance=4 (> k=3: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 1024; Rao M_t = 17
  m=4 t=2: length 16, |C_ext|=2^9 (<= 2*16^2=2^9), dual distance=6 (> k=5: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 32768; Rao M_t = 137
  m=4 t=3: length 16, |C_ext|=2^11 (<= 2*16^3=2^13), dual distance=8 (> k=7: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 1048576; Rao M_t = 697
  m=5 t=1: length 32, |C_ext|=2^6 (<= 2*32^1=2^6), dual distance=4 (> k=3: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 4096; Rao M_t = 33
  m=5 t=2: length 32, |C_ext|=2^11 (<= 2*32^2=2^11), dual distance=6 (> k=5: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 262144; Rao M_t = 529
  m=5 t=3: length 32, |C_ext|=2^16 (<= 2*32^3=2^16), dual distance=8 (> k=7: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 16777216; Rao M_t = 5489
  m=6 t=1: length 64, |C_ext|=2^7 (<= 2*64^1=2^7), dual distance=4 (> k=3: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 16384; Rao M_t = 65
  m=6 t=2: length 64, |C_ext|=2^13 (<= 2*64^2=2^13), dual distance=6 (> k=5: True); note's bound (2n)^ceil(k/2) = 2097152; Rao M_t = 2081
